Hanumān retells Citrakūṭa crow token as Sītā spoke it --- Crow tears Sītā breast and wakes bloodied sleeping Rāma --- Rāma fires Brahmā-bound darbha blazing like time fire at crow --- Reed chases Indra son through three worlds with no shelter --- Rāma shelters suppliant crow but blinds its right eye --- Sītā asks why mighty Rāma overlooks her and spares Rāvaṇa --- Hanumān swears Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa burn Laṅkā and fetch her home --- Sītā loosens braid knot and gives guarded crest jewel --- Weeping Sītā sends welfare to princes Sugrīva and begs swift rescue --- Hanumān bids Rāma trust Sītā loyal and well
